{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he saw the resting-place that it was good.</b> He saw that his portion was a blessed and good land for producing fruit." "<b>And he bowed his shoulder to bear.</b> The yoke of Torah." "<b>And he became.</b> To all his brothers, Israel — a leader." "<b>Tributary laborer.</b> To determine for them rulings of Torah and the reckonings of intercalation, as it is said ״וּמִבְּנֵי יִשָּׂשכָר יוֹדְעֵי בִינָה לָעִתִּים לָדַעַת מַה יַּעֲשֶׂה יִשְׂרָאֵל רָאשֵׁיהֶם מָאתַיִם״ (1 Chronicles 12) — two hundred heads of sanhedrin he established, and all their brothers at their word." "<b>And he bowed his shoulder.</b> He lowered his shoulder, as in ״וַיֵּט שָׁמַיִם״ (2 Samuel 22), ״הַטּוּ אָזְנְכֶם״ (Psalms 78). And Onkelos rendered it in a different sense: <b>And he bowed his shoulder to bear</b> — wars and to conquer districts, for they dwell on the border; <b>and he became</b> — the enemy subdued under him; <b>tributary laborer.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:10.499144798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}